# 4-bit ALU Using Verilog HDL

![Verilog](https://img.shields.io/badge/HDL-Verilog-blue)
![Simulation](https://img.shields.io/badge/Simulation-Icarus%20Verilog-green)
![Waveform](https://img.shields.io/badge/Waveform-GTKWave-orange)

## 📌 Project Overview

This project implements a **4-bit Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) using Verilog HDL**.

An ALU is an important digital circuit used in processors and digital systems. It performs arithmetic and logical operations on binary data.

The ALU designed in this project accepts two 4-bit input values and performs one of eight operations selected using a 3-bit control signal.

### Inputs

* `A` — 4-bit input
* `B` — 4-bit input
* `ALU_SEL` — 3-bit operation selection

### Outputs

* `Y` — 4-bit result
* `CARRY` — Carry/borrow indicator

---

## 🎯 Objectives

The objectives of this project are:

* To understand the working principle of an ALU.
* To design a 4-bit ALU using Verilog HDL.
* To implement arithmetic operations.
* To implement logical operations.
* To create a Verilog testbench.
* To verify all supported operations.
* To generate simulation waveforms using GTKWave.

---

## ⚡ ALU Operations

The 3-bit `ALU_SEL` signal selects the required operation.

| ALU_SEL | Operation | Function |
| :-----: | --------- | -------- |
|  `000`  | ADD       | `A + B`  |
|  `001`  | SUB       | `A - B`  |
|  `010`  | AND       | `A & B`  |
|  `011`  | OR        | `A \| B` |
|  `100`  | XOR       | `A ^ B`  |
|  `101`  | NOT       | `~A`     |
|  `110`  | INC       | `A + 1`  |
|  `111`  | DEC       | `A - 1`  |

---

## 🧱 Block Diagram

```text
                    +----------------------+
                    |                      |
        A[3:0] ---->|                      |
                    |                      |
        B[3:0] ---->|       4-BIT ALU      |-----> Y[3:0]
                    |                      |
  ALU_SEL[2:0] ---->|                      |-----> CARRY
                    |                      |
                    +----------------------+
```

