## 💻 Verilog Design

```verilog
`timescale 1ns/1ps

module alu4bit (
    input  wire [3:0] A,
    input  wire [3:0] B,
    input  wire [2:0] ALU_SEL,
    output reg  [3:0] Y,
    output reg        CARRY
);

    reg [4:0] temp;

    always @(*) begin

        Y = 4'b0000;
        CARRY = 1'b0;
        temp = 5'b00000;

        case (ALU_SEL)

            3'b000: begin
                temp = {1'b0, A} + {1'b0, B};
                Y = temp[3:0];
                CARRY = temp[4];
            end

            3'b001: begin
                Y = A - B;
                CARRY = (A < B);
            end

            3'b010: begin
                Y = A & B;
                CARRY = 1'b0;
            end

            3'b011: begin
                Y = A | B;
                CARRY = 1'b0;
            end

            3'b100: begin
                Y = A ^ B;
                CARRY = 1'b0;
            end

            3'b101: begin
                Y = ~A;
                CARRY = 1'b0;
            end

            3'b110: begin
                temp = {1'b0, A} + 5'b00001;
                Y = temp[3:0];
                CARRY = temp[4];
            end

            3'b111: begin
                Y = A - 4'b0001;
                CARRY = (A == 4'b0000);
            end

            default: begin
                Y = 4'b0000;
                CARRY = 1'b0;
            end

        endcase
    end

endmodule
```

---

## 🧪 Testbench

The testbench applies different input values and tests all eight ALU operations.

The following operations are tested:

```text
ADD
SUB
AND
OR
XOR
NOT
INC
DEC
```

An additional addition test is included to verify carry generation:

```text
1111 + 0001 = 1 0000
```

The 4-bit result is:

```text
0000
```

and the carry is:

```text
1
```

---

