------------------------------------------------------
10      0101    0011    000     1000    0
20      1001    0100    001     0101    0
30      1010    1100    010     1000    0
40      1010    1100    011     1110    0
50      1010    1100    100     0110    0
60      1010    0000    101     0101    0
70      0111    0000    110     1000    0
80      0111    0000    111     0110    0
90      1111    0001    000     0000    1
------------------------------------------------------
Simulation completed successfully.
======================================================
```

---

## 📈 Waveform

The testbench generates a VCD waveform file:

```text
alu4bit.vcd
```

The waveform contains:

```text
A
B
ALU_SEL
Y
CARRY
```

For example:

```text
A = 0101
B = 0011
ALU_SEL = 000

Y = 1000
CARRY = 0
```

This represents:

```text
5 + 3 = 8
```

Another example:

```text
A = 1010
B = 1100
ALU_SEL = 010

Y = 1000
```

This represents:

```text
1010 AND 1100 = 1000
```

---

## 🛠️ Tools Required

The project can be simulated using:

* Icarus Verilog
* GTKWave

Other Verilog simulators such as ModelSim, QuestaSim, or Vivado Simulator can also be used.

---

## ▶️ How to Run

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone <your-github-repository-url>
```

### 2. Enter the project directory

```bash
cd 4-bit-alu-verilog
```

### 3. Compile the Verilog files

```bash
iverilog -o alu_sim rtl/alu4bit.v tb/tb_alu4bit.v
```

### 4. Run the simulation

```bash
vvp alu_sim
```

### 5. Open the waveform

```bash
gtkwave alu4bit.vcd
```

Add:

```text
A
B
ALU_SEL
Y
CARRY
```

